 "text": "The pixy is a British folkloric figure, also spelled pigsy and piskie. The word names the Otherworldly beings of Fairyland. It is common in the West Country of England and in Cornwall. Pixies often wore green or red, had red hair and pointed ears, and were shorter than people. They squinted in daylight and preferred the night. They could be mischievous, leading people astray or rousing animals, but could also help with housework like Brownies.",
